  "preamble": "Nasalization of [u] to [ũ]. It arises either from a following nasal consonant that is later lost (Latin ūnum > Old Galician-Portuguese ũu > Portuguese um [ũ]) or spontaneously, as in Hindi pū̃ch 'tail' from Sanskrit púccha, where nasality appears without an etymological nasal.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Nasalization",
